Keep the Steam Deck IMU sampling while sensors are enabled.

The Deck samples its IMU by default, which is why the driver's SetSensorsEnabled did
nothing. The Steam client, however, writes SETTING_IMU_MODE off whenever Steam Input has
no gyro bound for the focused application, and again when its overlay closes. Steam runs
in the background on a Deck nearly all the time, so the driver kept decoding reports and
reporting sensor data, but every gyro and accelerometer field was zero and motion looked
dead.

Behind a new hint, SDL_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_STEAMDECK_IMU, write SETTING_IMU_MODE when sensors
are enabled, and write it again, at most once a second, while the reports keep showing an
all-zero IMU. The hint is off by default because the setting is Steam's to make while
Steam Input has the Deck, so nothing changes for anyone who does not ask for it. The IMU is
never switched off: sampling is the Deck's own default, and Steam or another reader may
rely on it.
diff --git a/src/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_steamdeck.c b/src/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_steamdeck.c
